{"ticker":"KSHINTL","symbol":"KSHINTL","instrumentId":3199641,"name":"Ksh International","industry":"NSE-Electrical-Power/Equipmt","about":"KSH International Limited is a manufacturer of magnet winding wires and continuously transposed conductors used in electrical and electromechanical applications. Its product range includes insulated rectangular and round wires engineered to customer-specific requirements. The company operates three state-of-the-art manufacturing facilities near Mumbai and Pune, equipped with advanced machinery and testing systems. It serves OEMs across power transmission and distribution, railway traction, motors, generators, transformers, renewables, electric vehicles, compressors, switchgear, pumps, and home appliances. KSH is a preferred supplier of continuously transposed conductors for extra-high-voltage power transformers, including HVDC and ultra-high-voltage applications. Operations are supported by certified quality, safety, and environmental management systems, with a strong focus on precision manufacturing, innovation, and consistent product performance.","website":"www.kshinternational.com","location":null,"exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:37:09.769Z","basis":"standalone","price":{"value":1056.2,"changePct":-1.0029056143968549,"week52High":1176.75,"week52Low":0},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹7,160 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹4,320 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"16,947,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"38"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"9,714,146"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.00%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"8.86"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.3"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"3.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.56"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.27"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-53%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"47.13"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"21–53"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"13.6%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value